---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const base = '/prisma-sql';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Configuration - prisma-sql"
  description="Generator fields, extension limits and strategy cost-model parameters, plus the programmatic tuning API."
  active={`${base}/docs/configuration`}
>
  <h1>Configuration</h1>
  <p>
    Tuning is optional. Defaults work without any configuration; knobs exist for schemas that need different safety
    boundaries or cost assumptions.
  </p>

  <h2>Generator configuration</h2>
  <pre><code>{`generator sql {
  provider   = "prisma-sql-generator"
  dialect    = "postgres"
  output     = "./generated/sql"
  skipInvalid = "true"
}`}</code></pre>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>provider</code></td><td>required</td><td>Use <code>prisma-sql-generator</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>dialect</code></td><td>inferred when possible</td><td><code>postgres</code> or <code>sqlite</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>output</code></td><td><code>./generated/sql</code></td><td>Generated SQL client output path</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>skipInvalid</code></td><td>false</td><td>Skip invalid @optimize directives instead of failing generation</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Extension config</h2>
  <p>Pass <code>limits</code> and/or <code>strategy</code> directly to <code>speedExtension</code>. Both accept partial objects.</p>
  <pre><code>{`const db = prisma.$extends(
  speedExtension({
    postgres: sql,
    limits: {
      MAX_INCLUDES_PER_LEVEL: 20,
      MAX_INCLUDE_DEPTH: 8,
    },
    strategy: {
      defaultFanOut: 5,
      roundtripRowEquivalent: 40,
    },
  }),
)`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Programmatic API</h2>
  <pre><code>{`import {
  setLimits, getLimits, resetLimits,
  setStrategyConfig, getStrategyConfig,
  rebuildQueryCache,
} from 'prisma-sql'

setLimits({ MAX_INCLUDES_PER_LEVEL: 25 })
rebuildQueryCache()   // required after changing QUERY_CACHE_SIZE
setStrategyConfig({ correlatedBoundedFactor: 0.3 })
resetLimits()`}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="limits">Query builder limits</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_INCLUDE_DEPTH</code></td><td>5</td><td>Max depth of nested include/select relations</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_INCLUDES_PER_LEVEL</code></td><td>10</td><td>Max relations included at one nesting level</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_TOTAL_SUBQUERIES</code></td><td>100</td><td>Total correlated subqueries allowed across the tree</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_SELF_REFERENTIAL_DEPTH</code></td><td>2</td><td>Max times a model can appear in its own include chain</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_QUERY_DEPTH</code></td><td>50</td><td>Max nesting depth for WHERE clauses</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_NOT_DEPTH</code></td><td>50</td><td>Max nesting depth for NOT composition</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_HAVING_DEPTH</code></td><td>50</td><td>Max nesting depth for HAVING clauses</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_NESTED_JOIN_DEPTH</code></td><td>10</td><td>Max depth for join-based relation traversal</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_RELATION_ORDER_BY_DEPTH</code></td><td>10</td><td>Max depth for relation orderBy resolution</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_WHERE_IN_RECURSIVE_DEPTH</code></td><td>10</td><td>Max recursion depth for where-in segment resolution</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_ARRAY_SIZE</code></td><td>10000</td><td>Max elements in array params such as in / hasSome</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_STRING_LENGTH</code></td><td>10000</td><td>Max string length for LIKE and JSON string operators</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_LIMIT_OFFSET</code></td><td>2147483647</td><td>PostgreSQL engine limit for LIMIT / OFFSET</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MIN_NEGATIVE_TAKE</code></td><td>-10000</td><td>Minimum allowed negative take value</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>MAX_ALIAS_COUNTER_THRESHOLD</code></td><td>1000</td><td>Safety threshold before alias counter overflow</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>QUERY_CACHE_SIZE</code></td><td>1000</td><td>Max entries in the SQL query cache (call rebuildQueryCache after changing)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>STMT_CACHE_SIZE</code></td><td>1000</td><td>Max entries in the SQLite prepared statement cache per client</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="strategy">Strategy cost-model parameters</h2>
  <p>These control how the planner chooses between query strategies.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>roundtripRowEquivalent</code></td><td>73</td><td>Cost in row-equivalents of one extra database roundtrip. Lower favors multi-roundtrip strategies.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>jsonRowFactor</code></td><td>1.5</td><td>Multiplier for JSON aggregation overhead per row</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>correlatedBoundedFactor</code></td><td>0.5</td><td>Cost factor for correlated subqueries when the child has LIMIT</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>correlatedUnboundedFactor</code></td><td>3.0</td><td>Cost factor for correlated subqueries when the child is unbounded</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>correlatedWherePenalty</code></td><td>3.0</td><td>Extra cost when a child relation has where inside a correlated subquery</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>defaultFanOut</code></td><td>10</td><td>Assumed average children per parent without stats</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>defaultParentCount</code></td><td>50</td><td>Assumed parent row count when take is not specified</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>dynamicTakeEstimate</code></td><td>10</td><td>Assumed take value when actual value is a runtime parameter</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>singleParentMaxFlatJoinDepth</code></td><td>2</td><td>Max include depth allowing flat-join for findFirst/findUnique</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>minStatsCoverage</code></td><td>0.1</td><td>Minimum relation stats coverage to trust collected data</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>largeChildTableRows</code></td><td>100000</td><td>Child table threshold for the large to-many include guard</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>smallParentCountThreshold</code></td><td>1000</td><td>Parent estimate threshold for the large to-many include guard</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Tuning examples</h3>
  <pre><code>{`// low-latency local database
speedExtension({ postgres: sql, strategy: { roundtripRowEquivalent: 20 } })

// remote database with high latency
speedExtension({ postgres: sql, strategy: { roundtripRowEquivalent: 200 } })

// large child tables that are well indexed
speedExtension({ postgres: sql, strategy: { largeChildTableRows: 500000 } })`}</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
